HL7 and FHIR
============

HL7®, HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN® and FHIR® are trademarks owned by Health Level Seven
International, registered with the United States Patent and Trademark Office.
This project is not affiliated with, sponsored or endorsed by Health Level
Seven International.

This software implements the HL7 Version 2 messaging standard (baseline
version 2.5.1) and produces resources conforming to HL7 FHIR Release 4
(version 4.0.1).

HL7 content in this software
----------------------------

Any HL7 Version 2 metadata in this software is limited to what the code needs
to parse, validate and convert messages: segment, field, data type and table
identifiers, their short names, structural rules (optionality, cardinality,
data types) and table codes. It is taken from these publications, which
Health Level Seven International releases under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0
Universal public domain dedication:

- HL7 Terminology (THO), https://terminology.hl7.org/
  HL7 Version 2 tables and code systems. THO is copyright (c) 1989+ Health
  Level Seven International.
- HL7 Version 2 to FHIR Implementation Guide, version 1.0.0 (STU 1),
  https://hl7.org/fhir/uv/v2mappings/
  Segment, data type and vocabulary mappings from HL7 Version 2 to FHIR R4.
- HL7 FHIR Release 4 (4.0.1), https://hl7.org/fhir/R4/
  FHIR resource definitions and code systems.

Where this software contains HL7 Terminology content it is a derivative work:
it includes only a subset of the codes, possibly in a different form, and it
is not the official HL7 Terminology.

No text of the HL7 Version 2 standard documents (definitions, descriptions,
usage notes) is reproduced. The HL7 Version 2 standard is available from
Health Level Seven International under its intellectual property policy.

Third-party terminologies
-------------------------

LOINC, SNOMED CT, UCUM and other external code systems are referenced only by
their identifiers and system URIs. This software contains none of their
content; their use is governed by their own licenses.
